IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dba-types`

-- Damage by Aircraft Act 1999 (Cth) — THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- The person on the ground asks: "Does the Act apply; who is liable to me;
-- can I recover without proving negligence; by how much are my damages
-- reduced if I was partly to blame?"

§ `Rules`

-- Endnote 3: Act No. 191, 2012, Schedule 1 item 7(3)-(4) — s 10(1A) and
-- s 11A apply to harm suffered on or after 31 March 2013.
`the 2013 amendments commence` MEANS Date 31 3 2013

-- s 4 (aircraft), s 9(2)-(4).
@ref ss 4, 9
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the aircraft for` h IF
        NOT (a's `a Defence Force aircraft`)
    AND NOT (a's `a model aircraft`)
    AND a's `within Australian territory`
    AND a's `an aircraft within s 9(4)`
    WHERE
        a MEANS h's `the aircraft`

-- s 10(1): harm caused by (a) an impact with an aircraft in flight, (b) with
-- part of one damaged in flight, (c) with something that dropped or fell
-- from one in flight, or (d) a result of such an impact. (1A): not for
-- mental injury alone (from 31 March 2013).
@ref s 10(1)-(1A)
@export Does s 10 of the Damage by Aircraft Act 1999 (Cth) apply to what happened to me? Yes if the harm was caused, within Australian territory, by an impact with an aircraft in flight (or just before), with part of one damaged in flight, or with something that fell from one in flight, or as a result of such an impact; not for a Defence Force or model aircraft, nor (from 31 March 2013) for mental injury alone. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`  @desc The aircraft, the cause, the kind of harm and its day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 applies to` h IF
        `the Act reaches the aircraft for` h
    AND NOT (h's `the cause` EQUALS `something else`)
    AND NOT (h's `only mental injury` AND h's `suffered on` AT LEAST `the 2013 amendments commence`)

-- s 10(2)(a)-(d), (2A), (3): who is jointly and severally liable.
@ref s 10(2)-(3)
@export Who is jointly and severally liable to me under s 10(2) of the Damage by Aircraft Act 1999 (Cth)? The operator; the owner, unless it had no active role and another person had the exclusive right to use the aircraft under a lease or arrangement or with the owner providing finance (s 10(2A)); the person who authorised the operator's use, if the operator lacked exclusive use for more than 14 consecutive days; and the person entitled to control navigation, if the operator used the aircraft without their authority and they had not taken all reasonable steps to prevent it. NOTHING where s 10 does not apply. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`  @desc The harm and the facts about the people involved
GIVETH A MAYBE `Persons liable`
`who is liable to me for` h MEANS
    IF `s 10 applies to` h
    THEN JUST (`Persons liable` OF TRUE, owner, authoriser, controller)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        p MEANS h's `the people`
        owner MEANS NOT (    NOT (p's `the owner had an active role in its operation`)
                         AND (p's `another had exclusive use under a lease or arrangement` OR p's `another had exclusive use with the owner financing`))
        authoriser MEANS p's `the operator was authorised to use it` AND NOT (p's `the operator had exclusive use for more than 14 consecutive days`)
        controller MEANS p's `the operator used it without the navigation controller's authority` AND NOT (p's `the navigation controller took all reasonable steps to prevent it`)

-- s 11: damages are recoverable "without proof of intention, negligence or
-- other cause of action".
@ref s 11
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I can recover without proof of fault for` h IF
    `s 10 applies to` h

-- s 11A(2)-(3): the damages but for my negligence "must be reduced to the
-- extent the court thinks just and equitable having regard to the share of
-- the sufferer in the responsibility". Taken as a reduction by that share
-- (F2); only for harm suffered on or after 31 March 2013.
@ref s 11A
@export My damages after a reduction for my own negligence under s 11A of the Damage by Aircraft Act 1999 (Cth): the damages the court finds but for my negligence, less my share of the responsibility as the court assesses it, not below nil. NOTHING where s 10 does not apply or the harm was suffered before 31 March 2013 (when s 11A began to apply). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`  @desc The harm, the court's damages and my share of responsibility
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my damages after contributory negligence for` h MEANS
    IF `s 10 applies to` h AND h's `suffered on` AT LEAST `the 2013 amendments commence`
    THEN JUST (h's `damages but for my negligence` TIMES (100 MINUS share) DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        share MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF h's `my share of responsibility, percent` GREATER THAN 100 THEN 100
                IF h's `my share of responsibility, percent` LESS THAN 0      THEN 0
                OTHERWISE                                                          h's `my share of responsibility, percent`

§ `The top-level goal`

@ref ss 4-11A
@export default The position under the Damage by Aircraft Act 1999 (Cth) of a person on the ground harmed by an aircraft: whether the Act applies (ss 9-10), who is jointly and severally liable (s 10(2)-(3)), whether damages are recoverable without proof of fault (s 11), and the damages after any reduction for my own negligence (s 11A). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `Harm case`  @desc The aircraft, the cause and harm, the people involved, and the court's findings on damages
GIVETH A `Aircraft harm position`
`the aircraft harm position for` h MEANS
    `Aircraft harm position` WITH
        `the Act applies`                               IS `s 10 applies to` h
        `who is liable`                                 IS `who is liable to me for` h
        `recoverable without proof of fault`            IS `I can recover without proof of fault for` h
        `damages after my contributory negligence`      IS `my damages after contributory negligence for` h
